### Specifically Verified Primary Citations

- **`Mugal2014`:** **Mugal, Wolf & Kaj (2014)**, *Why Time Matters: Codon Evolution and the Temporal Dynamics of dN/dS*, *Mol. Biol. Evol.* 31(1):212–231. DOI: [`10.1093/molbev/mst192`](https://doi.org/10.1093/molbev/mst192), PMCID: PMC3879453.  
  *Retained XML:* [`mugal_2014_temporal_dynamics_dnds.xml`](file:///home/leechuck/Documents/papers/empty-quarter-mags/resources/literature/darkmatter-2026-10-13/papers/round3/mugal_2014_temporal_dynamics_dnds.xml).  
  *Core Evidence:* Demonstrates continuous temporal decay of $dN/dS$ under mutation-selection-drift balance; unpurged transient polymorphisms at low $dS$ elevate $dN/dS$ toward 1.0, while stochastic ratio fluctuations cause severe instability at short timescales.
- **`AntiFam2012`:** **Eberhardt et al. (2012)**, *AntiFam: a tool to help identify spurious ORFs in protein annotation*, *Database* 2012:bas003. DOI: [`10.1093/database/bas003`](https://doi.org/10.1093/database/bas003), PMCID: PMC3308159.  
  *Retained XML:* [`eberhardt_2012_antifam_spurious_orfs.xml`](file:///home/leechuck/Documents/papers/empty-quarter-mags/resources/literature/darkmatter-2026-10-13/papers/round3/eberhardt_2012_antifam_spurious_orfs.xml).  
  *Core Evidence:* Details profile HMM identification of non-coding RNA translations (rRNAs, tRNAs) and opposite-strand artifacts that regularly enter protein databases from automated prokaryotic gene callers.
- **`Orr2026`:** **Orr & Bateman (2026)**, *Folding the unfoldable 2: using AlphaFold and ESMFold to explore spurious proteins*, *Bioinformatics Advances* 6(1):vbag160. DOI: [`10.1093/bioadv/vbag160`](https://doi.org/10.1093/bioadv/vbag160), PMCID: PMC13294457.  
  *Retained XML:* [`orr_2026_antifam_esmfold_spurious.xml`](file:///home/leechuck/Documents/papers/empty-quarter-mags/resources/literature/darkmatter-2026-10-13/papers/round3/orr_2026_antifam_esmfold_spurious.xml).  
  *Core Evidence:* Proves ESMFold and AlphaFold assign unexpectedly high pLDDT scores to short spurious AntiFam ORFs (<100 aa); discrimination improves only above 100 aa. Disparate pTM vs pLDDT indicates uncompacted non-globular models and shadow ORFs.
- **`tRNAscan-SE2`:** **Chan et al. (2021)**, *tRNAscan-SE 2.0: improved detection and functional classification of transfer RNA genes*, *Nucleic Acids Res.* 49(16):9077–9096. DOI: [`10.1093/nar/gkab688`](https://doi.org/10.1093/nar/gkab688), PMCID: PMC8450103.  
  *Retained XML:* [`chan_2021_trnascan_se2.xml`](file:///home/leechuck/Documents/papers/empty-quarter-mags/resources/literature/darkmatter-2026-10-13/papers/round3/chan_2021_trnascan_se2.xml).  
  *Core Evidence:* Upgrades tRNA annotation using Infernal 1.1 covariance models, specialized domain-specific models, and pseudo-tRNA filtering; primary tool for the 18-unique-tRNA MIMAG standard. (Foundational algorithm: Lowe & Eddy 1997, DOI: [`10.1093/nar/25.5.955`](https://doi.org/10.1093/nar/25.5.955), labelled inaccessible back-issue XML).
- **`skani`:** **Shaw & Yu (2023)**, *Fast and robust metagenomic sequence comparison through sparse chaining with skani*, *Nature Methods* 20(11):1661–1665. DOI: [`10.1038/s41592-023-02018-3`](https://doi.org/10.1038/s41592-023-02018-3), PMCID: PMC10630134.  
  *Retained XML:* [`shaw_2023_skani_sparse_chaining.xml`](file:///home/leechuck/Documents/papers/empty-quarter-mags/resources/literature/darkmatter-2026-10-13/papers/round3/shaw_2023_skani_sparse_chaining.xml).  
  *Core Evidence:* Sparse approximate chaining for robust ANI and aligned fraction calculation on fragmented, incomplete MAGs, defining the 95% species boundaries used in catalogue dereplication and MAG-to-isolate matching.
- **Additional Verified Citations:**
  - **Bakta:** **Schwengers et al. (2021)**, *Microb. Genom.*, DOI: [`10.1099/mgen.0.000685`](https://doi.org/10.1099/mgen.0.000685), PMCID: PMC8743544 ([`schwengers_2021_bakta_annotation.xml`](file:///home/leechuck/Documents/papers/empty-quarter-mags/resources/literature/darkmatter-2026-10-13/papers/round3/schwengers_2021_bakta_annotation.xml)).
  - **MIMAG Standards:** **Bowers et al. (2017)**, *Nat. Biotechnol.*, DOI: [`10.1038/nbt.3893`](https://doi.org/10.1038/nbt.3893), PMCID: PMC6436528 ([`bowers_2017_mimag_standards.xml`](file:///home/leechuck/Documents/papers/empty-quarter-mags/resources/literature/darkmatter-2026-10-13/papers/round3/bowers_2017_mimag_standards.xml)).
  - **FastTree 2:** **Price et al. (2010)**, *PLOS ONE*, DOI: [`10.1371/journal.pone.0009490`](https://doi.org/10.1371/journal.pone.0009490), PMCID: PMC2835736 ([`price_2010_fasttree2.xml`](file:///home/leechuck/Documents/papers/empty-quarter-mags/resources/literature/darkmatter-2026-10-13/papers/round3/price_2010_fasttree2.xml)).

