### Source-Grounded Methodological Cautions for the Manuscript

1. **AntiFam & Shadow ORFs (R2-06):**
   - *High-GC Mechanism:* High GC (median 70.9% in dark families) combined with RNY codon bias in authentic coding frames systematically eliminates stop codons in antisense frames $-1$ and $-2$ ([`larsen_2003_easygene_shadow_orfs.xml`](file:///home/leechuck/Documents/papers/empty-quarter-mags/resources/literature/darkmatter-2026-10-13/papers/round3/larsen_2003_easygene_shadow_orfs.xml)), generating long, non-coding shadow ORFs that Prodigal (`-p meta`) routinely mispredicts on truncated contigs ([`hyatt_2010_prodigal_gene_recognition.xml`](file:///home/leechuck/Documents/papers/empty-quarter-mags/resources/literature/darkmatter-2026-10-13/papers/round3/hyatt_2010_prodigal_gene_recognition.xml)).
   - *Selection on Shadow ORFs:* Standard $dN/dS$ is confounded in overlapping/antisense frames; apparent purifying selection is often an artifact of strong constraint on the primary gene ([`nelson_2020_olgenie_overlapping_genes.xml`](file:///home/leechuck/Documents/papers/empty-quarter-mags/resources/literature/darkmatter-2026-10-13/papers/round3/nelson_2020_olgenie_overlapping_genes.xml); [`ardern_2020_antisense_proteins_prokaryotes.xml`](file:///home/leechuck/Documents/papers/empty-quarter-mags/resources/literature/darkmatter-2026-10-13/papers/round3/ardern_2020_antisense_proteins_prokaryotes.xml)). AntiFam screening and geometric overlap filters ([`yooseph_2007_gos_shadow_orfs.xml`](file:///home/leechuck/Documents/papers/empty-quarter-mags/resources/literature/darkmatter-2026-10-13/papers/round3/yooseph_2007_gos_shadow_orfs.xml)) are mandatory quality controls.
2. **$dN/dS$ Time Dependence & Estimand Sensitivity (R2-04):**
   - Pairwise $dN/dS$ cannot be interpreted as constant selection strength without controlling for divergence time $dS$ ([`mugal_2014_temporal_dynamics_dnds.xml`](file:///home/leechuck/Documents/papers/empty-quarter-mags/resources/literature/darkmatter-2026-10-13/papers/round3/mugal_2014_temporal_dynamics_dnds.xml); Rocha 2006). Within-population $dN/dS$ is largely insensitive to selective intensity ([`kryazhimskiy_2008_population_genetics_dnds.xml`](file:///home/leechuck/Documents/papers/empty-quarter-mags/resources/literature/darkmatter-2026-10-13/papers/round3/kryazhimskiy_2008_population_genetics_dnds.xml)).
   - In P4, the matched difference sign is population-dependent (+0.012 weighted to dark families, −0.022 weighted to controls); stratum-specific medians must be presented primary. Short alignments (<100 aa) introduce severe stochastic counting variance (Nekrutenko 2002).
3. **Nucleotide Alignment vs. Protein Gene-Call Absence (R2-05):**
   - Reciprocal protein-protein BLAST failure does not indicate genomic absence. In close MAG-isolate pairs, 65.8% of dark calls lacking Bakta protein matches have high-identity DNA alignments in the isolate assembly.
   - Bakta ([`schwengers_2021_bakta_annotation.xml`](file:///home/leechuck/Documents/papers/empty-quarter-mags/resources/literature/darkmatter-2026-10-13/papers/round3/schwengers_2021_bakta_annotation.xml)) rigorously filters uncharacterized sORFs and spurious calls that Prodigal emits ab initio on MAGs, explaining the sharing gap. Direct nucleotide search or spliced protein-to-genome mapping with `miniprot` ([`li_2023_miniprot_protein_to_genome.xml`](file:///home/leechuck/Documents/papers/empty-quarter-mags/resources/literature/darkmatter-2026-10-13/papers/round3/li_2023_miniprot_protein_to_genome.xml); [`tonkin_hill_2020_panaroo_pangenome_polishing.xml`](file:///home/leechuck/Documents/papers/empty-quarter-mags/resources/literature/darkmatter-2026-10-13/papers/round3/tonkin_hill_2020_panaroo_pangenome_polishing.xml)) is required before asserting accessory status.
4. **Structural Score Normalisation & Spurious Predictions (R2-02, R2-03):**
   - The 2.26% structural control floor was an artifact of 66 extended single alpha-helices ($R_g = 4.79\times$ expected) failing Foldseek's 3Di prefilter due to low information density ([`vankempen_2024_foldseek_structure_search.xml`](file:///home/leechuck/Documents/papers/empty-quarter-mags/resources/literature/darkmatter-2026-10-13/papers/round3/vankempen_2024_foldseek_structure_search.xml)). Excluding zero-row models yields 2.6% dark vs 0.07% control no-hits.
   - Query-normalised TM-score penalizes multi-domain proteins; 77.3% of whole-query no-hits align at $TM_{aligned} \ge 0.5$ over $\ge 100$ residues ([`lau_2024_ted_encyclopedia_of_domains.xml`](file:///home/leechuck/Documents/papers/empty-quarter-mags/resources/literature/darkmatter-2026-10-13/papers/round3/lau_2024_ted_encyclopedia_of_domains.xml); [`lau_2023_merizo_domain_segmentation.xml`](file:///home/leechuck/Documents/papers/empty-quarter-mags/resources/literature/darkmatter-2026-10-13/papers/round3/lau_2023_merizo_domain_segmentation.xml)). Novelty claims must be restricted to compact, segmented domains.

No manuscript or analysis files were altered. All items in the prompt are verified and complete.
